Wait for every bulk transfer to come back before rtlsdr_read_async frees them

A change to librtlsdr, osmocom/rtl-sdr at 797f8143266d, written for Revenant and
distributed under librtlsdr's own licence, GPL-2.0-or-later, like the file it
modifies. git apply skips this preamble.

When rtlsdr_read_async was cancelled, it cancelled each transfer whose last
status was not CANCELLED, and returned on the first pass in which no
libusb_cancel_transfer call succeeded. A transfer libusb is already
cancelling answers LIBUSB_ERROR_NOT_FOUND until its completion has been
handled, and its status field still holds its previous completion, so that
pass could come while transfers were still in flight. read_async then freed
them and returned -5, and libusb wrote to the freed memory afterwards, in
windows_iocp_thread or in add_to_flying_list under the next control transfer.
Measured on Windows with libusb 1.0.29 at about one cancel in three hundred.

With this change the callback resubmits only while streaming, every transfer
is counted in flight from submission until libusb hands it back through the
callback, and the cancel waits on libusb's events until that count is zero.
If event handling itself fails with transfers still out, they are leaked
rather than freed.

Revenant: docs/rtlsdr-provenance.md, "The librtlsdr the engine links".

